{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Therefore the Torah grows faint (תפוג)</b> — like: \"his heart grew faint (ויפג לבו)\" (Genesis 45:26). As long as a person is alive, his heart beats within him; but when they said to him, \"Joseph is alive,\" his heart stopped and did not beat, because he was overwhelmed — like: \"do not cause to faint (אל תתני פוגת).\" And the proof: \"the spirit of Jacob their father revived (ותחי רוח יעקב אביהם)\" (Genesis 45:27)." "And the meaning of <b>תפוג</b>: the Torah ceases — as if there is no law of Torah in the world." "<b>Surrounding (מכתיר)</b> — surrounding, from the root of כתר (crown), which is round. And Yefet said: for the wicked surrounds the righteous — and this is what the prophet spoke concerning Nebuchadnezzar, who killed the pious. And now his prophecy begins."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {2 "The phrase 'ועתה החל נבואתו' is ambiguous: 'his prophecy' may refer to Nebuchadnezzar's onslaught or to the prophet Habakkuk's prophecy; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:52.203119489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}